, ...`, Python `\\N{...}`, `HYPHEN-MINUS`, `DIGIT FIVE`) | gap (gap unicode-character-names) | yes | upper-case words `LATIN SMALL LETTER`, `SPACE`, `COMMA`, `COLON`, `EXCLAMATION MARK` separated by `,`/`;`/newline; or `\\N{` | `unicodedata.lookup(name)` per token (stdlib); `\\N{}` -> `codecs.decode(t,'unicode_escape')` | high: \"every character has a name\" = D25 sequel |\n| 174 | code-point notation knobs: braces `\\u{4E}` (ES6/Ruby/Swift), `\\x{4E}` (Perl), `U+4E` short, lowercase `u+004e`, no separators `U+004EU+0069`, comma/newline lists, decimal/octal code points with prefixes (`0d78`, `#78`, `0o116`), `&#x...;` per astral char, `\\N{U+004E}` | gap (gap codepoint-notation-knobs) | yes | any token family `<prefix><digits>` one per char | tokenise `(?:[Uu]\\+\\|\\\\[uUx]\\{?\\|%u\\|0x\\|0d\\|0o\\|&#x?)([0-9A-Fa-f]+)\\}?;?`, radix from the prefix, `chr`; whole text must be tokens | high: D25 knob (\"Same point ...\") |\n| 175 | code-point ARITHMETIC: every code point + constant K (Caesar on code points, crib gives K), shifted into another block (fullwidth +0xFEE0, Tags +0xE0000, halfwidth, enclosed/negative-squared letters U+1F130/1F170), XOR mask on code points | gap (gap codepoint-offset-block) | yes (crib) | text of ONE non-ASCII block, or `U+` tokens decoding to junk whose ord - ord(crib) is constant | K = ord(t[0]) - ord('N'); verify on the crib; letter-only blocks need a per-case base (A/a); NFKC for compatibility forms | high: \"point\" arithmetic, cheap Unicode pun |\n| 176 | invisible Unicode smuggling: Tags block U+E0020-E007E (ASCII smuggling), variation selectors as bytes (VS1-16 U+FE00-FE0F = 0-15, VS17-256 U+E0100-E01EF = 16-255) after a carrier emoji, Unicode noncharacters/PUA as bytes | gap (gap unicode-tag-smuggling) | yes | blob that renders as one emoji/word but is hundreds of bytes; `\\U000e00xx` / `\\ufe0x` runs | tags: `chr(cp - 0xE0000)`; VS: `cp-0xFE00` or `cp-0xE0100+16` -> bytes -> UTF-8 | high: AI-arena-topical \"invisible prompt\" tric