; NULs in a non-LE/BE 4-byte pattern -> middle-endian; d8xx dcxx -> surrogates, then NFKC;\n   pairs/quads swapped -> byte-swap words; base64 with AG/AA rhythm -> b64 then utf-16-le; LSB-first bits\n . - only (+ / or 3 spaces) ....... Morse (D16: output only 0-9A-F -> hex layer; digits -> char codes); 1/111 runs -> timing\n a/b (A/B) in 5s .................. Baconian (D17: all groups start `a` -> values 0-15 = HEX nibbles, 2 per byte);\n                                    values up to 25 -> letters; odd casing in cover text -> Bacon via case\n ANY 16-symbol output (0-9A-F, a-p only, 16 words) after a carrier = hex nibbles -> fromhex (D16, D17);\n   unknown 16 tokens -> map them by the crib hex `4e 69 63 65 20 77 6f 72 6b`. lib: twosym/bin4/aphex/tern/radix_dec\n 2-symbol groups of width 5/6 with values >15 -> base32/base64 INDEX;  ䷀.. hexagrams -> base64;  only space/TAB -> bits\n dotted quads/#RRGGBB/4e69:6365 -> IPv4/colour/IPv6 bytes; b64-ish won't decode -> undo rev/rot13 1st (U4fV=rot13 H4sI)\n %XX .............................. URL (D7);  &#..; -> HTML (D8);  \\uXXXX -> JSON (D9);  \\xNN -> C escape\n U+004E U+0069 (D25, 7 B/char) / %uXXXX / \\U0000XXXX / \\u{4E} -> chr(int(h,16)); mixed prefixes -> one alternation tokenizer\n   LATIN SMALL LETTER I / \\N{..} -> unicodedata.lookup;  =XX / soft \"=\\n\" -> quoted-printable;  =?UTF-8?B?..?= -> MIME\n N:c,N:c, ... digits:payload, ..... NETSTRINGS (D24, every len 1): count-cursor parse, never split(','); payload `,`/`:`\n   are data (1:,, 1::,). No comma -> bencode (l..e, i..e)/sexp; tag ,#!~^]} -> tnetstring; $len CRLF -> RESP; hex len -> chunked\n A-Z2-7 (=) ....................... base32 (D10);  0-9A-V -> base32hex;  ybndrfg8.. -> z-base-32;  no ILOU -> Crockford\n A-Za-z0-9+/ (=), len%4==0 ........ base64 (D1); H4sI = GZIP inside (D21: base64 -d | gzip -dc); eN = ZLIB 78da (D22:\n   zlib.decompress(b64decode(t)); eJ/eF/eA other levels; zlib = (b0<<8|b1)%31==0, not just 0x78; no magic -> wbits=-15);\n   Qlpo bz2, /Td6WFo xz, KLUv/ zstd, UEsDB zip, N3q8 7z, U2FsdGVkX1 openssl, .eJ flask cookie, eyJ JWT -> never score bytes\n A-Za-z0-9-_ no = ................. base64url (D11);  [0-9A-Za-z] only, no pad -> base62 (x1.34) / base36 one case (x1.55)\n no 0 O I l + / = -> base58 (x1.37);  0-9A-Z plus space $%*+-./: -> base45 (x1.5)\n <~ ... ~> around ! .. u ......... ASCII85 (D23): a85decode(t,adobe=True); no <~ -> a85decode (z = 4 NULs);\n   RFC1924 set (no quotes , . / : [ \\ ]) -> b85decode; .-:+=^!/*?&<>()[]{}@%$# -> Z85; xbtoa Begin -> btoa\n ~all printable, no ' - \\ ......... basE91 (x1.23);  ! .. } minus \" ` -> base92;  no chunk structure -> bignum radix\n begin 644 / lines start M or h ... uuencode / xxencode;  xn-- labels -> punycode/IDNA;  ADFGX(V) only -> ADFGVX (key: title word + crib);  A C G T only -> DNA 2-bit / codon\nNON-ASCII:\n U+2800-28FF ⠝⠊⠉⠑ ................. Braille (⠼ = number sign)\n fullwidth Ｎｉｃｅ / math 𝐍𝐢𝐜𝐞 / ⓝ -> NFKC;  ɐ q ɔ p ǝ ɟ ƃ ɥ ᴉ ʞ ɯ ɹ ʇ ʌ ʍ ʎ -> upside-down (from_upside_down, maybe [::-1])\n CJK U+7Cxx + spaces -> ROT8000; dense CJK/Hangul -> base65536/2048; emoji 1/byte -> base100; CJK U+xx00 -> swap bytes\n zero-width U+200B/C/D/2060/FEFF -> bits; U+E00xx tags -> cp-0xE0000; FE00../E0100.. selectors -> bytes; one block with\n   ord-ord(crib) constant -> code-point offset; runes/Greek/Cyrillic, lengths kept -> crib map; Cyrillic look-alikes -> homoglyph\nSAME LENGTH, LETTERS ONLY CHANGE (word lengths 4 4 8 4 6! ... kept):\n best rot-N English -> Caesar (D2 rot13, D14 +7); digits also +5 -> ROT18/ROT5;  mirror a<->z -> Atbash (D13)\n crib c-p constant ratio .......... affine (lib _fit_affine); constant per position mod k -> Vigenere key = (c-p)\n crib c+p periodic -> Beaufort (primer then plaintext -> autokey);  crib map consistent, not affine -> keyword subst\n neighbour keys (Muvr eptl) ....... QWERTY shift;  ;,.' in words -> Dvorak;  ALL printables shift -> ROT47 (D15)/ROT8000\nSAME CHARACTER MULTISET (anagram: one ! , :, slug digits intact) = TRANSPOSITION (D12 reverse, D18 rail 3):\n rail fence (D18: number in prompt = rails; w.rail_solve) | redefence | scytale/columnar (w.col_solve) | route/Caesar box\n | skip k | riffle | word order. Strip only \\r\\n (spaces are ciphertext); accept only text STARTING `Nice work`\nWORDS: Alfa Bravo -> NATO; -ay -> Pig Latin; N1c3 w0rk -> leet. Title pun -> key: cipher + number = key (D18 \"Three rails\")\n\"Same ...\"/\"Another ...\"/\"This time ...\" (D20, D22) = yesterday's codec, ONE knob turned; \"alphabet got bigger\" (D23) = base-N size\nMastery: line k = day k's codec; keyed/transposed lines restart the key PER LINE (D18: 6-8 char rail-3 slug tail);\n lines 19/20 own BOM, 21/22 own gzip/zlib, 23 own `<~..~>`, 24 own `1:c,`, 25 own `U+XXXX`. NEVER pre-decode a line (D23,\n D25: all NN wrong) -- register_free(name, TODAY'S DAY, fn) on the RAW line even if the whole-blob step decodes single/TT.\n STACKS (D16-17, D19-21): output hex/digits/b32/a-p/NUL-rhythm/compressed-magic bytes -> decode AGAIN. Solver: return on the first full slug; slow fallbacks only on a miss.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"unicode-character-names\", \"concept\": \"Unicode character NAMES per character (`LATIN CAPITAL LETTER N, LATIN SMALL LETTER I, SPACE, ...`, `\\\\N{...}`)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Most likely D25 sequel ('every character has a point' -> 'has a name'). Decoder names_dec(t): split on , ; newline | or detect `\\\\N{..}`; each token -> unicodedata.lookup (case-insensitive, also aliases like 'HYPHEN-MINUS', 'FULL STOP', 'DIGIT FIVE'); whole text must resolve or None. Also accept `U+004E LATIN CAPITAL LETTER N` (UnicodeData.txt line style) and lowercase names. Register in CANDIDATES + decode_chunk + as a free codec for Mastery fragments (5-10 names per line). Fixtures: comma list, newline list, \\\\N{} string, UnicodeData lines, decoys (English prose in caps).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"codepoint-notation-knobs\", \"concept\": \"code-point notation knobs: `\\\\u{4E}`, `\\\\x{4E}`, short `U+4E`, lowercase `u+`, no separators, decimal/octal code points with prefixes, `\\\\N{U+004E}`\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D26 knob on D25 (U+XXXX uppercase 4-hex, single spaces). Extend uplus_dec into codepoints_any(t): tokenizer `(?:[Uu]\\\\+|\\\\\\\\[uUx]\\\\{?|%u|0x|0d|0o|0b|&#x?|\\\\\\\\N\\\\{U\\\\+)([0-9A-Za-z]+)\\\\}?;?` with radix from the prefix; tokens may be adjacent (no separator) or separated by space , ; newline; whole text must tokenise. Fixtures: each prefix form, adjacency, astral (U+1F600), mixed case; decoys: plain hex, `0x` C arrays of BYTES (must still route to hex/char-code decoders: gate on slug).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"codepoint-offset-block\", \"concept\": \"code-point arithmetic: constant offset K over every code point (Caesar on code points), text shifted into another Unicode block, XOR mask on code points\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Crib makes it keyless: K = ord(t[0]) - ord('N') (or from the first U+ token), verify K on the whole 87-char crib. Cover: generic +K (incl. K < 0 and K moving ASCII into CJK/PUA/astral), fullwidth (+0xFEE0, space -> U+3000), Tags (+0xE0000), enclosed/squared/negative-squared Latin (letter base per case, digits separate), math alphanumerics (per-style base table; NFKC handles most), XOR K on code points. Fixtures per block + U+ token form of a shifted text + decoys (ROT8000 must still route to rot8000).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"unicode-tag-smuggling\", \"concept\": \"invisible Unicode smuggling: Tags block (U+E0020-E007E) ASCII smuggling and variation-selector byte smuggling (U+FE00-FE0F, U+E0100-E01EF) after a carrier emoji\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"AI-arena-topical 'invisible instruction' encodings. tags_dec: keep chars in U+E0000-E007F -> chr(cp-0xE0000) (drop U+E0001 language tag / U+E007F cancel). vs_dec: VS1-16 -> 0-15, VS17-256 -> 16-255, bytes -> UTF-8 (Paul Butler emoji smuggling); ignore the visible carrier chars. Must read the artifact as UTF-8 (astral). Fixtures: tags after visible text, tags alone, emoji+VS, mixed with zero-width (zero-width decoder must not steal), decoys (real emoji sequences with VS16 U+FE0F only).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mixed-escape-soup\", \"concept\": \"every character in a randomly chosen notation (U+004E, \\\\u0069, &#99;, &#x65;, %20, \\\\x77, 0x6f, \\\\162, named entities)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Likely Time Trial / Mastery MUTATION of the D7/D8/D9/D25 codecs ('new unseen effects'). One alternation tokenizer over URL %xx, %uXXXX, HTML &#N; &#xH; &name;, \\\\uXXXX, \\\\UXXXXXXXX, \\\\u{..}, \\\\xNN, \\\\NNN octal, U+XXXX, 0xNN; whole text must tokenise (allow single separators); per-token radix. Prefer stdlib (html.unescape, unquote) only after splitting. Fixtures: uniform random mixtures, per-word notation, with and without separators; decoys: single-notation blobs (must give the same text).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"rhythm-broken-structure-first\", \"concept\": \"when the day is a NEW family with no charset fingerprint, read the blob's structure first\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D24 broke the D19-D23 'new family, then one knob' rhythm (no Ascii85 knob; framing instead), and nothing prebuilt covered it. Worker rule: if STEP 1 (lib) misses, describe the repeating unit (here '\\\\d+:.,' x 111) and name the spec from it + the title pun before brute-forcing codecs; write a strict whole-text parser that returns None on mismatch so it can sit first in the pipeline. D25 confirmed the pattern (third new family in a row: code points, a D9 sibling); the prebuilt row-22 decoder caught it, so keep the queue wide across families.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-line-routing\", \"concept\": \"Mastery: every day's codec must claim its RAW line inside decode_chunked / _joint_free\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23 Mastery lost its first submit (113/113 sets: right slug words, wrong NN, every digit +5): the solver pre-decoded line 23 ('<~..~>' -> 'el-46') in place, and the joint free-codec search -- which has no identity option -- gave the plain line a digit ROT5. Rule: never rewrite numbered lines before decode_chunked; add the day's codec via register_free(name, day, fn) (gated to its own charset/delimiters) or decode_chunk. Before any timed start, print one set's joined sentence and check the slug digits against the single-solve shape. Same fields wrong on every set = one line's routing. D24 confirmed the rule: _netstr registered as register_free('netstr', 24, ...) and skipped as a whole-blob step for numbered blobs -> Mastery 118 x 24 first try. D25 REPEATED the bug through another path (123/123 sets NN wrong): _uplus_lines pre-decoded line 25 and, with no day-25 codec registered, decode._positional sent the plain line to _unknown_line_cands, which re-decoded it. Checklist for every new day: (1) register_free(name, day, fn) for TODAY's day number; (2) the whole-blob step must skip numbered Mastery blobs; (3) print one set's joined sentence and compare NN with the raw last line before submitting.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"byte-family-mastery-cost\", \"concept\": \"Mastery solve time per set as codecs accumulate; lane-solver continuity\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D21 Mastery (103 x 21) died at the 60 s harness budget because solve.py was an ad-hoc generic per-line brute force, not the carried D20 lane solver; the D20 solver + one `_b64z` branch did 0.34 s. D22 Mastery (108 x 22) passed first try with the D21 solver unchanged (plus the solverrt partial-emit wrapper) but solve took 15.9 s and submit 11.8 s -- profile per set if it grows; D23 (113 x 23) solved in 1.2 s. Rule: copy the previous day's solve.py, add today's codec as one whole-blob step + register_free(name, day, fn), return early, time hctf solver-test on the real Mastery case before any timed start. D24 (118 x 24): solve 1.6 s, whole Mastery 4.5 s. D25 (123 x 25): solve 0.76 s.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"netstring-knobs\", \"concept\": \"netstring knobs: len > 1 and mixed lengths, len in UTF-8 bytes vs characters, leading zeros, whitespace/newlines between frames, missing final comma, nested netstrings, frames whose payload is a seen codec\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild ok). Most likely D25 knob on D24 'String Theory' (1-char netstrings). Generalise warmups_codecs.netstr_dec into netstr_any(t): cursor over BYTES (t.encode('utf-8')) and over chars, both tried; allow optional whitespace/newline between frames and a missing final ','; leading zeros in len; if every payload is itself a netstring run, recurse; if payloads are not English, run decode_chunk on each payload AND on the joined payload (frames of base64/hex/rot13). Whole text must parse or return None. Register in CANDIDATES + decode_chunk + as a free codec for 8-40 char Mastery fragments. Fixtures: len 1 / 2-9 / random mixed, UTF-8 multibyte payload (byte vs char), nested, b64-per-frame, decoys (plain prose with '3:' times).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"indexed-fragments-shuffled\", \"concept\": \"index-tagged frames out of order (`17:a,3:b`, `a@17`, `[17]a`) and run-count frames (`3:o,` = 'ooo')\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild ok). 'Count carefully' re-read: the number before ':' may be a POSITION (frames shuffled; sort by index, check 0..n-1 or 1..n with no gaps/repeats) or a REPEAT COUNT (RLE: payload char x N). netstring len and count read the same when all N=1, so decide by N > 1 with a 1-char payload (count) or by a permutation of range(n) (index). Build frames_dec(t) trying netstring -> index-sort -> run-count, slug-gated. Fixtures: shuffled index frames (0- and 1-based, separators , ; space), RLE colon form 'N:c,' and 'c*N', decoys.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"tnetstrings\", \"concept\": \"tnetstrings (typed netstrings): `<len>:<data><tag>` with tags , string # int ^ float ! bool ~ null ] list } dict\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild ok). Sibling spec of D24 (Zed Shaw's typed netstrings). Recursive cursor parser: len, ':', len chars, one tag char; ']' / '}' payloads parse recursively; collect string leaves in order (and dict values) and join; slug-gate. Cue: netstring shape whose terminators vary over ',#^!~]}'. Fixtures: flat strings, a list of 1-char strings, a dict {i: char}, nested.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bencode-sexp\", \"concept\": \"bencode (`4:spam`, `i42e`, `l..e`, `d..e`) and Rivest canonical/transport S-expressions (`(3:abc5:hello)`, `[3:mime]`, `{base64}`, `|b64|`, `#hex#`)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild ok). Same 'len:data' atom as netstrings but NO trailing comma (BitTorrent bencode; SPKI canonical sexp). Cursor parser: digits ':' -> string of len; 'i'..'e' int; 'l'..'e' list; 'd'..'e' dict (key/value strings in order); sexp '(' ')' lists with optional '[display-hint]', transport forms {b64 of canonical} |b64 atom| #hex atom#. Join string leaves; slug-gate. Fixtures: bencoded list of 1-char strings, one long string, dict, canonical sexp, transport {..} form.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"length-prefix-binary-tlv\", \"concept\": \"binary length prefixes under hex/base64: Pascal strings, u16/u32 BE/LE lengths, varint (protobuf string field), TLV (type+len+value), hex-digit lengths\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild ok). Framing x the byte family (D19-D22 had byte-level knobs). After any hex/b64 decode, try: 1-byte len frames; 2/4-byte BE/LE len; LEB128 varint len (lib has LEB128); 1-byte type + 1/2-byte len (TLV); protobuf wire (tag byte 0x0a etc. + varint len); hex-digit len text frames ('0e' + data). Whole stream must parse; join payloads; slug-gate. Fixtures: one char per frame and one frame per word, each width/endianness, TLV with alternating type bytes, decoys (plain hex of text).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"delta-encoded-codepoints\", \"concept\": \"delta / chained code points: first absolute then signed differences, running XOR, cumulative sums\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Point to point' re-read. Integer token lists (decimal, signed, or U+/hex) whose values are mostly small and signed: try cumulative sum, XOR scan (c_i = v_i ^ c_{i-1}), and the reverse direction; chr; crib-gated (must START 'Nice work'). Fixtures: signed decimal deltas, hex deltas mod 256 / mod 0x110000, XOR chain hex, decoys (plain decimal char codes must not be re-summed).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"utf8-bytes-mojibake\", \"concept\": \"UTF-8 bytes vs code points: mojibake (UTF-8 read as cp1252/latin-1, double-encoded), byte escapes of multibyte sequences\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Encoding confusion' sibling of D19-D20 and D25. Detect Ã/Â/ï¼/â€ runs; repair by t.encode('cp1252' or 'latin-1', errors='strict').decode('utf-8') repeated up to 3 times; then NFKC and the normal pipeline (fullwidth text survives as ASCII). Also `\\\\xef\\\\xbc\\\\xae` / `%EF%BC%AE` byte escapes -> bytes -> utf-8. ftfy not installed -- stdlib only. Fixtures: single/double mojibake of fullwidth and of plain text with smart quotes, cp1252 vs latin-1 differences (0x80-0x9F).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"script-letter-map-crib\", \"concept\": \"letter maps into another SCRIPT (runes, Greek, Cyrillic, Ogham, Deseret, Shavian, Tifinagh, Old Italic)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Non-Latin glyphs from one block with the crib's word lengths kept. First standard transliteration tables (Elder Futhark, Greek ISO 843-ish, Cyrillic GOST/ISO 9, Ogham, Deseret phonetic is NOT 1:1 -- keep as low), then generic crib mapping: glyph->letter from the 87-char crib (21 letters), unknown glyphs f j q y z resolved by the slug word list (adj-noun-noun from earlier days' slugs). Fixtures per script + a random-glyph-alphabet substitution.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"float-encoded-charcodes\", \"concept\": \"floating / fixed point numbers carrying char codes (IEEE-754 float32/64 hex, decimals 78.0, scaled fixed point, packed floats in base64)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'You Have a Point' read as decimal/floating point. Tokens 0x429c0000 (float32 BE of 78.0) / 16-hex doubles / '78.0' / '0.78' / '7.8e1'; base64 of packed '<f'/'>d' arrays. struct.unpack both endians, round, chr; fixed point: detect common scale 10^k or 2^k; crib-gated. Fixtures each + decoys (plain decimal codes).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"case-and-digit-loss\", \"concept\": \"case-losing / digit-losing codecs (Morse, NATO, Polybius, tap, Bacon, A1Z26, T9)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Output must be lowercased; A1Z26/Polybius/Bacon/tap have no digit symbols, so slug digits are passed through literally or spelled - the decoder must keep non-alphabet tokens verbatim. Lowercase only the FINAL text, and test a collapsed output for an inner hex/digit layer first (D16 Morse -> UPPERCASE hex, D17 Bacon -> a-p).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"transposition-mastery-joint\", \"concept\": \"short Mastery fragments under a transposition (6-8 chars, key restarts per line)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D18 line 18 ('p-pr5e6' -> 'pper-56') has no charset cue; decode_chunked misses it (a D21 generalize worker's intermediate run left 'Master:i rbsk-...'). Keep the slug-gated per-line rail pass; register any future transposition decoder as a free codec with its day number so _joint_free tries it on each unclaimed line.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"affine-free-strict\", \"concept\": \"affine as a GM-confirmed-ready free codec\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Already prebuilt (wc:affine + SPECULATIVE_FREE + _fit_affine). Risk is only bigram ranking vs rot-N/Atbash in Mastery joint assignment; confirm ratchet path registers it with a day number on first sight.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"chepy-cyberchef-cue\", \"concept\": \"standard-tool fallback for any unseen encoding\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"chepy (venv) has from_base45/58/62/85/91/92/65536, rot_8000, from_upside_down, decode_zero_width, from_fullwidth, from_bacon, from_braille, from_nato, sms_decode_multitap, vigenere_decode, bifid_decode, gzip/zlib/bzip/lzma/lz4/lz77 _decompress, raw_inflate, unzip_all, tar_extract_all; CyberChef ops at tools/npm-cyberchef/node_modules/cyberchef/src/core/operations (Magic recipe finds compression layers).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"string-builder-literals\", \"concept\": \"'String' as code: concatenated string literals, String.fromCharCode / chr() calls, char arrays, ''.join([...]), JSON/Python lists of characters\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild ok). Title-pun sibling of D24 ('String Theory'). Never eval: regex/ast.literal_eval only on literal-only nodes. Forms: \\\"Ni\\\" + \\\"ce\\\" (JS/Java/C#), Python implicit 'N' 'i', String.fromCharCode(78,105,...), chr(78)+chr(105), new char[]{'N','i'}, [char]78+[char]105 (PowerShell), ''.join(['N','i']), [\\\"N\\\",\\\"i\\\"] JSON, b'\\\\x4e' bytes literals. Extract literal pieces in order, unescape, join; slug-gate. Overlaps lib.scripts deobfuscators -- reuse them. Fixtures per language + decoys.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"resp-redis\", \"concept\": \"RESP (Redis serialization protocol) bulk/simple strings and arrays\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild ok). Length-prefixed 'string protocol' sibling: '*<n>\\\\r\\\\n' arrays, '$<len>\\\\r\\\\n<data>\\\\r\\\\n' bulk strings, '+text\\\\r\\\\n', ':int\\\\r\\\\n', RESP3 '=' verbatim. Cursor parser tolerant to bare '\\\\n'; join bulk strings; slug-gate. Fixtures: array of 1-char bulk strings, one bulk string per word, CRLF vs LF.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"http-chunked-transfer\", \"concept\": \"HTTP/1.1 chunked transfer encoding as a text framing (hex chunk sizes, CRLF, final 0 chunk, chunk extensions)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild ok). Framing with HEX lengths ('Count carefully' in base 16). Parser: read hex size up to ';' or CRLF, take size bytes, expect CRLF, loop until size 0; tolerate LF-only and missing trailer. Optionally Content-Encoding gzip/deflate on the dechunked body (reuse magic sniff). Fixtures: 1-char chunks, word chunks, extensions, gzip body.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"asn1-der-tlv\", \"concept\": \"ASN.1 DER/BER TLV strings (UTF8String 0c, OCTET STRING 04, PrintableString 13, IA5String 16, SEQUENCE 30) in hex/base64/PEM\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild ok). Standard TLV framing. Minimal stdlib walker: tag byte, short/long-form length, recurse into constructed (0x20 bit) types, collect string leaves in order, join; slug-gate. Cues: hex '30 81'/'30 82'/'0c'+len, base64 'MI'/'MD'/'DA'. asn1crypto may not be importable in the solver -- keep it stdlib. Fixtures: SEQUENCE of 1-char UTF8Strings, one OCTET STRING, BER indefinite length.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"delimited-field-framing\", \"concept\": \"CSV/TSV quoted fields with doubled-quote escapes, Lisp char lists, YAML flow sequences carrying one char or word per field\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild ok). Delimiter-escaping sibling of netstrings (the payload contains the delimiter, escaped instead of counted). csv.reader for '\\\"N\\\",\\\"i\\\",\\\"\\\"\\\"\\\"' (doubled quote), TSV with \\\\t escapes, Scheme #\\\\N char literals, YAML flow [N, i, ' ']. Join fields; slug-gate. Fixtures each + decoys.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"figlet-ascii-art-text\", \"concept\": \"ASCII-art / dot-matrix rendering of the sentence (figlet banners, 5x7 bitmaps as #/. rows or hex rows)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Points'/'pixels' pun; less likely (the slug must be machine-readable). pyfiglet is NOT installed: vendor 2-3 standard figlet fonts (standard, banner, big) as glyph tables, segment glyphs by blank columns (or fixed width), match exactly; 5x7 dot-matrix: standard HD44780 font table, rows as #/. or hex. Fixtures: figlet standard of the sentence, banner font, 5x7 '#' rows, hex rows.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bifid-adfgvx\", \"concept\": \"Bifid / Trifid / ADFGX / ADFGVX / Nihilist\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"pycipher implements all; key from title; ADFGX cue is the 5/6-letter alphabet.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mime-encoded-word\", \"concept\": \"MIME encoded-word headers\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"email.header.decode_header handles =?charset?B|Q?...?=. Body-level MIME wrappers are in text-armor-wrappers.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"esoteric\", \"concept\": \"Brainfuck / Ook! (Chuck Norris unary is prebuilt: chuck_dec)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"No bf interpreter installed; a 20-line stdlib interpreter or pip 'brainfuck-interpreter' if one ever appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"misc-tables\", \"concept\": \"chemical symbols, Cetacean, Citrix CTX1 (DNA/codon, Roman, BCD, Gray, Kenny are prebuilt in warmups_codecs)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Recognition cues only; each is a lookup table the worker can write in one turn; CyberChef has From BCD and Cetacean Cipher Decode.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"homoglyph\", \"concept\": \"homoglyph (Cyrillic/Greek look-alike) substitution\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"unidecode/confusables not installed; NFKC does not fold Cyrillic. Install unidecode only if a day uses it.\"}\n]\n```\n","numLines":157,"startLine":180,"totalLines":336}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016BfKXh9MMREJcDdd2PSgL7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
