{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E5aoVRuHPNguAfDMnQAKJ1","type":"tool_result","content":"def _unknown_line_cands(frag):\n    \"\"\"Every decoding of a line whose day has no known codec (today's, before anyone registered it), most literal\n    first: the fragment VERBATIM, the strict chunk decoders and every lib.warmups_codecs.CANDIDATES decoder that\n    re-encodes to the exact bytes, then all rot-N / Atbash / reversal, then the speculative free codecs. The template +\n    known-slug check in _positional_ok picks among them; a tie keeps the earlier (more literal) one.\n    D25: solve.py had pre-decoded line 25 to `le-52`; the speculative codecs came first and `rot18`'s `le-07` won the\n    tie (same slug words; bigrams don't see digits) -> 123/123 Mastery sets wrong.\"\"\"\n    out = []\n\n    def add(x):\n        if isinstance(x, str) and x and x not in out:\n            out.append(x)\n    add(frag)\n    add(decode_chunk(frag))\n    try:\n        from lib import warmups_codecs as W\n        for _name, enc, dec in W.CANDIDATES:\n            if dec is None:\n                continue\n            p = W.safe(dec, frag)\n            if p is not None and p not in out:\n                try:\n                    if enc(p) == frag:\n                        out.append(p)\n                except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 - an encoder that doesn't apply to this text\n                    pass\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        pass\n    for n in range(1, 26):\n        add(_rot(frag, n))\n    add(_atbash(frag))\n    add(frag[::-1])\n    for x in _free_cands(_SPEC, frag):\n        add(x)\n    return out\n\n\ndef _positional(rows):\n    \"\"\"Warmups Mastery puts line k under day k's codec. Decode each line with ITS day's codec (lib.warmups_codecs.DAYS,\n    else a free codec registered for that day, else a strict self-identifying chunk) and require every line to\n    re-encode to its exact bytes. Free codecs re-encode anything, so the caller also requires the template + a slug of\n    known words. Right on 295/295 verified Mastery sets D1-D14 where the joint guess misses ~0.6% of random sets.\n    -> [candidate texts]: one, or one per decoding of the single LAST line whose day has no codec yet (today's).\n    [] = numbering isn't 1..N, a line fails its codec, or more than the last line is unknown (-> the joint path).\"\"\"\n    if not POSITIONAL or [k for k, _ in rows] != list(range(1, len(rows) + 1)):\n        return []\n    try:\n        from lib import warmups_codecs as W\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        return []\n    out = []\n    for k, frag in rows:\n        c = W.day_codec(k)\n        if c:\n            p = W.safe(c[2], frag)\n            if p is None or c[1](p) != frag:\n                if k == len(rows):\n                    # the last line fails its own day codec = a solver already decoded it (D25 `U+...` -> `le-52`,\n                    # registered as day 25 by that night's ratchet): read it as unknown, verbatim first\n                    out.append(_unknown_line_cands(frag))\n                    continue\n                return []\n            out.append([p])\n            continue\n        fn = next((f for _n, d, f in _FREE if d == k), None)\n        if fn:\n            cands = fn(frag)\n            p = cands[0] if cands else None\n        elif k == len(rows):\n            p = None\n            out.append(_unknown_line_cands(frag))\n            continue\n        elif not _free_line(frag):\n            p = decode_chunk(frag)\n        if p is None:\n            return []\n        out.append([p])\n    head = \"\".join(x[0] for x in out[:-1])\n    return [head + last for last in out[-1]]\n\n\ndef _positional_ok(rows):\n    \"\"\"The positional reading that is the template + a slug whose three words are all known, else None. With several\n    (an unknown last-line codec): the VERBATIM last line when it already completes the template (a plain fragment is\n    nev