een D26\nrep(\"| 83 | Brainfuck / Ook! | gap | yes | `+-<>[].` / `Ook. Ook?` | bf interpreter (none installed) | low: program, not encoding |\",\n    \"| 83 | Brainfuck / Ook! | seen D26 (Brainfuck: only `+ - .`, ONE cell, signed-delta runs then `.`, no loops/`<>`, no newline, 3406 B = ~31 B per char; Mastery line 26 = 5-char tail, 166-217 B; D26 solver `_bf` = step-capped pure-python interpreter, whole-blob step; Mastery routing still broken: DAYS encoder != GM bytes); Ook!/dialects -> row 183 | yes | `+-<>[].` only, runs of one sign + `.`; `Ook. Ook?` | running sum of `+`/`-` read at `.` (loop-free one cell); else `_bf` | done (single/TT); Mastery line 26 needs `register_free(\\\"bf\\\",26)`; knobs -> rows 183-184 |\")\n\n# 3. new table rows after row 182\nanchor = s.index(\"| 182 | floating / fixed point\")\neol = s.index(\"\\n\", anchor) + 1\nrows = \"\"\"| 183 | Brainfuck TOKEN dialects: Ook! (`Ook. Ook?` pairs), Blub (`Blub. Blub?`), COW (`moo mOo MOo ...` 12 cmds), Pikalang (`pi ka pipi pichu ...`), ReverseFuck (signs swapped), Alphuck, Roadrunner (`Meep`), Binaryfuck/3-bit, custom 8-word maps | gap (gap bf-token-dialects) | yes (std tables; custom map via crib) | 2-3 distinct words repeated in fixed pairs (Ook), 8-12 distinct tokens with BF-like run structure | token -> BF char table, then `_bf`; unknown 8-token map: assign tokens so the program prints `Nice work` | high: \"same language, other words\" = D27 knob |\n| 184 | full Brainfuck programs: loops (`++++++++[>+++++++++<-]>++.` multiplication generators), many cells `<>`, comment/prose text between commands, wrap below 0, `,` input, 16-bit cells, BF under a seen wrapper (base64/hex/gzip of BF) | gap (gap bf-full-programs; D26 `_bf` already runs loops) | yes | `[`/`]`/`<`/`>` present; BF chars embedded in English; b64 that decodes to `+-<>[].` soup | strip non-commands only when the remaining program prints a slug; interpreter with step cap 10^7, 30000+ cells, 8-bit wrap | high: knob on D26 |\n| 185 | Deadfish (`i` +1, `d` -1, `s` square, `o` output; 256/-1 reset to 0) and XKCD variant (`x k c d`) | gap (gap deadfish) | yes | only `i d s o` (or `x k c d`), long `i` runs then `o` | 6-line interpreter with the 256/-1 -> 0 rule | high: \"very small language\" taken literally (4 cmds) |\n| 186 | Whitespace language (stack program in space/tab/LF; push = `SS` + sign + binary + `L`, print char = `TLSS`), also visible `S T L` / `[Space][Tab][LF]` notation | gap (gap whitespace-language) | yes | blob of only ` `, `\\\\t`, `\\\\n` (or `S`/`T`/`L` letters) with `SS..L` pushes | parse IMP/commands, run stack/heap/IO subset, step cap; whitespace-stego (row 106) must not steal it | med-high: \"say nothing\" / \"silent\" pun |\n| 187 | Befunge-93/98, ><> (2-D grid languages): `\"....\"` string mode pushes chars, `,`/`o` output, `>v<^` flow, `@`/`;` end | gap (gap befunge-2d) | yes | multi-line grid with `v` `<` `^` `>` `@` and a quoted reversed string | grid interpreter (stack, string mode, `#` bridge, `_`/`|` ifs) with step cap | med: \"think in two dimensions\" |\n| 188 | JSFuck (`[]()!+` only), aaencode (`ﾟωﾟﾉ= /｀ｍ´）ﾉ ~┻━┻`), jjencode (`$=~[];$={___:++$...`) | gap (gap jsfuck-aaencode) | yes | 6-char alphabet; Japanese emoticons; `$=~[]` | NEVER node/eval: static pure-python evaluator of the JSFuck algebra (`+[]`=0, `![]`=false, `([]+{})`...) / known regex decoders for aa/jj | med: \"small alphabet language\" sequel |\n| 189 | Chef / Shakespeare / other prose-shaped languages (recipe: ingredients = values, `Put X into the mixing bowl`, `Pour contents of the mixing bowl into the baking dish`, `Serves 1.`; SPL `Act I`, `You are as ... as`) | gap (gap chef-recipe-lang) | yes | a cooking recipe / play with numeric ingredient amounts and a `Method.` section | Chef subset interpreter (stack bowls, Pour = output in pop order); SPL: noun/adjective arithmetic subset | med: \"Food for Thought\" sequel (\"recipe\", \"cook\", \"serves\") |\n| 190 | toy stack-VM / assembly / one-liner listings that print chars: `PUSH 78 / OUT`, Forth `78 emit`, dc `78P`, PostScript, `mov al,0x4e` + `int 10h`, HQ9+-like, Unary/Lenguage counts | gap (gap stack-vm-listing) | yes | mnemonics with small ints 32-126, one per output char | tokenise and simulate a generic push/add/sub/mul/out machine (never execute real code); count-based langs only if the count is small | med: \"small language\" re-read |\n| 191 | Malbolge (self-modifying, base-3 crazy op, `(=<\\\\`#9]~6ZY32Vx/4Rs+0No-&Jk)\"Fh}|Bcy?`=*z]Kw%oG4UUS0/@-ejc(:'8dc`) | gap (gap malbolge) | yes | printable soup starting `(=<` / `('&%` with no structure | reference interpreter (~40 lines: xlat1/xlat2 tables, crazy op), step cap | low-med: \"hell\"/\"eighth circle\" pun |\n\"\"\"\ns = s[:eol] + rows + s[eol:]\n\n# 4. recognition cues\nrep(\"\"\"WORDS: Alfa Bravo -> NATO; -ay -> Pig Latin; N1c3 w0rk -> leet. Title pun -> key: cipher + number = key (D18 \"Three rails\")\n\"Same ...\"/\"Another ...\"/\"This time ...\" (D20, D22) = yesterday's codec, ONE knob turned; \"alphabet got bigger\" (D23) = base-N size\n\"\"\", \"\"\"WORDS: Alfa Bravo -> NATO; -ay -> Pig Latin; N1c3 w0rk -> leet. Pun -> key (D18 \"Three rails\"); \"Same/Another\" = 1 knob\nPROGRAMS (\"language\", D26): + - . runs only = Brainfuck -> RUN it (running sum at `.`; loops -> `_bf`, step cap, never node)\n Ook./Ook? Blub. MoO pi/ka -> BF token map; i d s o -> Deadfish; only space/TAB/LF pushes -> Whitespace; \"..\",@ v>^ -> Befunge\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\" lines 19/20 own BOM, 21/22 own gzip/zlib, 23 own `<~..~>`, 24 own `1:c,`, 25 own `U+XXXX`. NEVER pre-decode a line (D23,\n D25: all NN wrong) -- register_free(name, TODAY'S DAY, fn) on the RAW line even if the whole-blob step decodes single/TT.\n\"\"\", \"\"\" lines 19/20 own BOM, 21/22 gzip/zlib, 23 `<~..~>`, 24 `1:c,`, 25 `U+XXXX`, 26 BF from cell 0. NEVER pre-decode a line (D23,\n D25: all NN wrong); register_free(name, TODAY'S DAY, fn) on the RAW line -- a DAYS entry must round-trip (D26 timeout).\n\"\"\")\n\n# 5. readiness gaps JSON\nm = re.search(r\"## Readiness gaps\\n\\n```json\\n(.*?)\\n```\", s, re.S)\ngaps = json.loads(m.group(1))\ngaps = [g for g in gaps if g[\"id\"] != \"esoteric\"]\nbuilt_now = {\"unicode-character-names\", \"codepoint-notation-knobs\", \"codepoint-offset-block\", \"unicode-tag-smuggling\",\n             \"mixed-escape-soup\", \"delta-encoded-codepoints\", \"utf8-bytes-mojibake\", \"script-letter-map-crib\",\n             \"float-encoded-charcodes\"}\nfor g in gaps:\n    if g[\"id\"] in built_now:\n        if not g[\"detail\"].startswith(\"BUILT\"):\n            g[\"detail\"] = \"BUILT (prebuild ok). \" + g[\"detail\"]\n        g[\"priority\"] = 2 if g[\"id\"] in {\"mixed-escape-soup\", \"unicode-tag-smuggling\", \"codepoint-offset-block\"} else 3\n    if g[\"id\"] == \"mastery-line-routing\":\n        g[\"detail\"] += (\" D26 broke it a THIRD way: the solver appended a runtime warmups_codecs.DAYS entry (26, 'brainfuck', \"\n            \"enc='+'*ord(c)+'.>', _bf) whose encoder does not reproduce the GM's one-cell DELTA bytes; _positional's re-encode \"\n            \"check rejected line 26 on all 128 sets -> _unknown_line_cands + joint search per set -> solve 64.9 s, 0 answers \"\n            \"(harness kill); a live worker hand-decoded and submitted. (4) A DAYS entry must round-trip a REAL Mastery line \"\n            \"(assert enc(dec(line)) == line) -- many-to-one codecs (programs, whitespace/padding variants) go through \"\n            \"register_free instead; (5) time hctf solver-test on a real Mastery case before the timed start.\")\n    if g[\"id\"] == \"rhythm-broken-structure-first\":\n        g[\"detail\"] += (\" D26 made it four new families in a row and the prompt named a LANGUAGE: a blob with a tiny operator \"\n            \"alphabet (`+ - .`) and run structure is a PROGRAM -> interpret it (pure python, step cap), don't table-decode.\")\nnew = [\n {\"id\": \"mastery-bf-line-26\", \"concept\": \"carried solver: Mastery line 26 (Brainfuck) must be routed by a decode-only registration\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"The D26 solver/ still times out on Mastery (DAYS[26] encoder = absolute '+'*ord per cell; GM = one-cell signed deltas, runs of one sign then '.', restarting at 0 per line). Tomorrow's copied solver must, BEFORE anything else: replace the runtime DAYS append with decode.register_free('bf', 26, lambda p: [x for x in [_bf(p)] if x]) (or an encoder emitting the delta form: v=0; for c: d=ord(c)-v; out+=('+'*d if d>0 else '-'*-d)+'.'; v=ord(c)), then hctf solver-test the variant-mastery-ca7796e4 case (128 x 26) and check < 5 s.\"},\n {\"id\": \"bf-token-dialects\", \"concept\": \"Brainfuck token dialects: Ook!, Blub, COW, Pikalang, ReverseFuck, Alphuck, Roadrunner, Binaryfuck/3-bit, custom 8-token maps\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Most likely D27 knob ('same language, other words'; Ook! is the canonical BF sibling). bf_dialect_dec(t): Ook (tokens 'Ook.'/'Ook?'/'Ook!' paired: '. ?'='>' '? .'='<' '. .'='+' '! !'='-' '! .'='.' '. !'=',' '! ?'='[' '? !'=']'; also short Ook '.?' pairs without the word), Blub (same pairing), COW (moo mOo moO mOO Moo MOo MoO MOO OOO MMM OOM oom; MoO=+, MOo=-, moO=>, mOo=<, Moo=out-or-in, MOO/moo loops), Pikalang (pipi=>, pichu=<, pi=+, ka=-, pikachu=., pikapi=,, pika=[, chu=]), ReverseFuck (+/- and </> swapped), Alphuck (a c e i j o p s), Binaryfuck/3-bit (000..111 per command), Roadrunner (Meep variants). Then the D26 _bf interpreter. Unknown token set of <= 8 distinct words with run structure: assign tokens to +-.<>[], by the crib (the program must print 'Nice work') -- brute 8! only over tokens seen. Register in CANDIDATES + decode_chunk + register_free for 5-char Mastery fragments. Fixtures: each dialect encoding the sentence with the GM's D26 delta style AND with loops; decoys (English prose, Morse).\"},\n {\"id\": \"bf-full-programs\", \"concept\": \"full Brainfuck: loops/multiplication generators, many cells, comment text between commands, wrap below 0, ',' input, 16-bit cells, BF under a seen wrapper\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Knob on D26 (only + - . seen). Move the D26 solver's _bf into lib.warmups_codecs.bf_run(prog, steps=10**7, cells=65536, bits=8) + bf_dec(t): accept when, after removing non-command chars, the program has balanced brackets and >= 1 '.', run it, printable + slug gate; try 8-bit wrap first, then 16-bit/unbounded cells if output is junk; ',' reads 0 (or EOF=-1 variant). Also peel: if a base64/hex/gzip decode yields BF soup, run it (stack with decompress-then-redecode). Encoders for fixtures: D26 delta style, multiplication-loop generator (n = a*b + c per char), cell-per-char with '>' and a shared 10x loop (the common 'bf text generator' output). Decoys: Morse lines (. - space) must not be claimed unless the program output passes the slug gate.\"},\n {\"id\": \"deadfish\", \"concept\": \"Deadfish (i d s o; value reset to 0 at 256 or -1) and the XKCD variant (x k c d)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'A very small language' read literally (4 commands, output = the number, or chr(number) in the char variant). deadfish_dec(t): only [idso] (or [xkcd]) + whitespace; v=0; i +1, d -1, s v*v, o -> chr(v) (char-output variant, what a text-printing challenge needs; also collect numbers and try chr); after each op, v in {-1, 256} -> 0. Also accept uppercase. Fixtures: delta style (i/d runs then o) and square-based style (s to jump), XKCD letters; decoys: English words made of i/d/s/o only ('dido') must fail the slug gate.\"},\n {\"id\": \"whitespace-language\", \"concept\": \"Whitespace programming language (space/tab/LF; also visible S/T/L or [Space][Tab][LF] notation)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Esolang sibling of D26. ws_dec(t): keep only ' ', '\\\\t', '\\\\n' (or map S/T/L letters, [Space]/[Tab]/[LF] tokens); parse IMPs: SS push (sign S=+ T=-, binary S=0 T=1, L end), SLS dup, SLT swap, SLL drop, TSSS add, TSST sub, TSSL mul, TLSS output char, TLST output num, LSS label, LSL call, LLL end, etc.; run with a step cap; join output. Must sit BEFORE whitespace-stego (row 106) and zero-width decoders, and those must stay as fallbacks. Fixtures: push+print per char (typical generator output), with labels/loops, visible S/T/L notation; decoys: whitespace stego blobs (8-bit space/tab).\"},\n {\"id\": \"befunge-2d\", \"concept\": \"Befunge-93/98 and ><> (2-D grid languages)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"befunge_dec(t): grid 80x25 (or text bounds), PC starts (0,0) moving right; implement 0-9 + - * / % ! ` > < ^ v ? (deterministic: treat ? as >) _ | \\\" : \\\\\\\\ $ . , # g p & ~ @ ; string mode pushes ords; ',' outputs chr; step cap 10^6. ><>: o outputs, ; ends, ' and \\\" strings, mirrors / \\\\\\\\ | _ #. Fixtures: the common '\\\"!dlrow olleH\\\">:#,_@' style generator for the sentence, multi-line v/< loops, ><> version; decoys: ASCII art (row 181).\"},\n {\"id\": \"jsfuck-aaencode\", \"concept\": \"JSFuck ([]()!+ only), aaencode (Japanese emoticons), jjencode ($=~[] style) -- JS-from-tiny-alphabet encodings\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"NEVER node/eval (untrusted program). JSFuck: a pure-python evaluator for the JSFuck expression algebra (values: [], ![], +[], []+[], string indexing, [][\\\"flat\\\"] -> function source text constants, Function('return ...')() for the final string; implement the ~40 primitives the jsfuck.com encoder uses) and read the string passed to the final call (eval/Function body) -- usually alert(\\\"...\\\") or the bare string. aaencode/jjencode: known static decoders (regex the per-char octal/hex digit expressions, e.g. aadecode by replacing the emoticon digit symbols) -> the JS source -> extract the string literal. Fixtures from a vendored encoder (pure python port) for the sentence; decoys: base64/ROT47 soups.\"},\n {\"id\": \"chef-recipe-lang\", \"concept\": \"Chef (recipe-shaped language) and Shakespeare (play-shaped) programs that print text\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Food for Thought' -> 'recipe' pun risk. chef_dec(t): parse 'Ingredients.' (amount [measure] name; amounts = char codes), 'Method.' steps: Put X into [the] [nth] mixing bowl (push), Fold, Add/Remove/Combine/Divide, Liquefy [contents of the] mixing bowl (mark as chars), Pour contents of the [nth] mixing bowl into the [nth] baking dish, 'Serves N.' (output dishes, top of stack first = REVERSED push order); loops 'Verb the ingredient.' ... 'Verb until verbed.' with a step cap. Shakespeare: subset (characters, 'You are as <adj> as <noun>' arithmetic = powers of 2, 'Speak your mind!' outputs chr). Fixtures: the common 'Hello World Souffle' style generator for the sentence; decoys: plain English recipes without Method.\"},\n {\"id\": \"stack-vm-listing\", \"concept\": \"toy stack-VM / assembly / one-liner listings that print characters (PUSH 78 / OUT, Forth 78 emit, dc 78P, PostScript, mov al,0x4e; HQ9+)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'A very small language' read as a tiny instruction set. vm_dec(t): tokenise lines into mnemonic + int args (decimal/hex/char literal); simulate a generic machine: PUSH/LOAD/MOV/SET n, ADD/SUB/INC/DEC/MUL, OUT/PRINT/PUTC/EMIT/WRITE/P/INT 0x10 (print low byte or top of stack), JMP/LOOP only with a step cap; Forth 'n emit', dc 'nP' / 'n P', PostScript '(..) show'. Output gate: printable + slug. NEVER execute as real code. Fixtures: 4-5 synthetic dialects (stack, register, Forth, dc, 8086-ish) printing the sentence; decoys: decimal char-code lists (D5 must still win).\"},\n {\"id\": \"malbolge\", \"concept\": \"Malbolge programs (self-modifying, ternary crazy op)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Reference interpreter (~40 lines): memory 59049 trits-words, initialise from program (whitespace skipped, chars validated by (c + i) % 94 in the allowed set), fill rest with crazy(m[i-1], m[i-2]); ops by (c + i) % 94: 4 jmp, 5 out chr(a % 256), 23 in, 39 rotr, 40 mov d, 62 crazy, 68 nop, 81 end; encrypt with xlat2 after each step; step cap 10^7. Cue: printable soup starting '(=<`' / \\\"('&%\\\" with no b64/b85 structure. Fixtures: a known Malbolge program for a short text (generate with a vendored pure-python Malbolge generator if one fits in ~150 lines, else hand-include published hello-world style programs and accept fixtures for shorter strings).\"},\n]\nids = {g[\"id\"] for g in gaps}\nfor g in new:\n    assert g[\"id\"] not in ids, g[\"id\"]\ngaps = new[:1] + [g for g in gaps if g[\"priority\"] == 1] + new[1:] + [g for g in gaps if g[\"priority\"] != 1]\ngaps.sort(key=lambda g: g[\"priority\"])\nbody = \"[\\n\" + \",\\n\".join(\"  \" + json.dumps(g, ensure_ascii=False) for g in gaps) + \"\\n]\"\njson.loads(body)\ns = s[:m.start(1)] + body + s[m.end(1):]\nopen(p, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s)\nprint(len(gaps), sum(1 for g in gaps if g[\"action\"] == \"prebuild\"))\nPYEOF\npython3 -I $TMPDIR/atlas26/edit.py reference/coverage/warmups.md","description":"Apply atlas edits and rebuild gap JSON"}}}
